      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The mechanistic underpinning involves the LNP's sophisticated interaction with endosomal trafficking, where the ionizable lipid's $\\text{pKa}$ tuning to $6.4$ facilitates protonation within the acidic endosome, inducing a destabilization of the endosomal membrane via the \"proton sponge effect.\" This facilitates the release of the nucleoside-modified mRNA payload into the cytosol, bypassing lysosomal degradation pathways. The structural architecture, governed by the stoichiometric balance of cholesterol (membrane rigidity modulator), PEG-lipid (steric stabilization against opsonization), and DSPC (bilayer scaffolding), dictates the particle's pharmacokinetics and endosomal escape efficiency. This controlled release mechanism ensures high translational fidelity of the encoded antigen within the antigen-presenting dendritic cells, concurrently mitigating immunopathology associated with excessive systemic cytokine release.",
      "source": "target",
